 "blockers": [],
 "notes": [
  "Community commands take the community UUID, not the slug. Find it in the 'id' field of search-communities, list-featured-communities or get-record-communities. Examples: eu = f0a8b890-f97a-4eb2-9eac-8b8a712d3a6c, dockstore = f312c6b6-0dd6-4fb2-a224-7c4960394ac1, biosyslit = c529f97d-f8cb-4c13-a439-9e36891694c2.",
  "Record ids are the numeric part of zenodo.org/records/{id}. links.parent_doi gives the concept DOI, which list-citing-works needs; strip the https://doi.org/ prefix first.",
  "robots.txt disallows the global /search page and direct /api/records URLs. search-records replays the XHR the record page makes. If it gets blocked, use search-community-records with a q query scoped to a community.",
  "Search responses include hits.total and aggregations (facet counts for resource_type, access_status, etc.) next to hits.hits.",
  "list-citing-works queries an external host (zenodo-broker.web.cern.ch) and often returns zero hits for new records.",
  "All commands are anonymous reads. Nothing here needs a login."
 ],
